WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:16.272
"Hey!" I exclaimed, blurting out my story idea.

2
00:00:16.273 --> 00:00:20.906
"Let's write a story about a giant talking vacuum cleaner.

3
00:00:20.907 --> 00:00:26.103
It can suck up the whole world!"

4
00:00:26.104 --> 00:00:29.064
"Huh?" Molly blinked at me.

5
00:00:29.065 --> 00:00:31.041
Then she shook her head.

6
00:00:31.042 --> 00:00:34.873
"No, Iggy. The vaccum cleaner sounds like a monster.

7
00:00:34.874 --> 00:00:39.345
I'm not writing a story about a monster!"

8
00:00:39.346 --> 00:00:42.805
At lunch we talked some more about my idea.

9
00:00:42.806 --> 00:00:46.062
Molly kept pointing out problems with it.

10
00:00:46.063 --> 00:00:51.539
"The giant vacuum cleaner can't suck up the whole world, Iggy," she said.

11
00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:56.561
"If it did, there wouldn't be a story because nothing would be left."

12
00:00:56.562 --> 00:01:00.726
I knew Molly was right.

13
00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:06.550
I decided that thinking of a plot for a story was even harder than inventing!

14
00:01:06.551 --> 00:01:10.083
Other kids were talking about plot ideas too.

15
00:01:10.084 --> 00:01:16.093
"Mrs. Romano said we should bounce our ideas off each other," said Colby.

16
00:01:16.094 --> 00:01:21.093
"Boing!" said Jake, bouncing a grape off Colby's head.

17
00:01:21.094 --> 00:01:26.839
"She said to bounce story ideas, not food!" said Kristin.

18
00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:33.505
After school we stopped at Molly's apartment to ask if Molly could come to my apartment.

19
00:01:33.506 --> 00:01:40.370
Caswell and Lucy were in the living room, watching Monster Madness again.

20
00:01:40.371 --> 00:01:43.524
Lucy just stared at the TV screen.

21
00:01:43.525 --> 00:01:47.227
"Iggy, your mom wants to see you and Molly right away.

22
00:01:47.228 --> 00:01:50.783
She has a surprise."

23
00:01:50.784 --> 00:01:54.183
Molly and I raced over to my apartment.

24
00:01:54.184 --> 00:01:57.949
"What's the surprise, Mom?" I blurted out.

25
00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:01.140
"I can't tell you yet," said Mom.

26
00:02:01.141 --> 00:02:03.485
"But we're going somewhere fun.

27
00:02:03.486 --> 00:02:06.888
Caswell can come too, if he wants."

28
00:02:06.889 --> 00:02:12.514
Caswell decided he could miss the rest of Monster Madness for today.

29
00:02:12.515 --> 00:02:18.926
Soon all of us, including Lucy, were walking down the busy street.

30
00:02:18.927 --> 00:02:24.649
We passed Bubbles Bath Shop and waved to Mr. Chen.

31
00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:30.657
We passed our school and waved to Mrs. Romano, who was just leaving for the day.

32
00:02:30.658 --> 00:02:36.052
At last my mom stopped in front of a shop I had never seen before.

33
00:02:36.053 --> 00:02:39.739
A sign read: "Garden Gate Children's Bookstore.

34
00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:42.410
Author Story Hour Today!"

35
00:02:42.411 --> 00:02:46.086
"It's a new bookstore," my mom explained.

36
00:02:46.087 --> 00:02:49.897
"And we're just in time for story hour."

37
00:02:49.898 --> 00:02:55.869
We entered through a door that looked like a garden gate.

38
00:02:55.870 --> 00:03:01.549
Kids were sitting on the floor, and a lady was sitting on a chair in front of them.

39
00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:05.260
"I'm Matilda Mackey," she said.

40
00:03:05.261 --> 00:03:12.292
"I'm going to read my new book, The Wicky Wacky School."

41
00:03:12.293 --> 00:03:17.247
Matilda Mackey's book was about a school where weird things happen.

42
00:03:17.248 --> 00:03:23.897
One day the teachers turn into monkeys, and the main character has to figure out how to change them back.

43
00:03:23.898 --> 00:03:30.730
She solves the problem when she realizes the teachers have been eating too many bananas.

44
00:03:30.731 --> 00:03:35.688
I thought the story was really funny and had a lot of suspense.

45
00:03:35.689 --> 00:03:38.686
Suddenly I got an idea.

46
00:03:38.687 --> 00:03:41.064
I leaned over to Molly.

47
00:03:41.065 --> 00:03:45.752
"Maybe Mrs. Mackey can help us think of a plot for our story!"

48
00:03:45.753 --> 00:03:49.762
Molly nodded and gave me the thumbs-up sign.

49
00:03:49.763 --> 00:03:54.653
After Mrs. Mackey finished reading, Molly and I rushed up to her.

50
00:03:54.654 --> 00:03:58.977
"My name is Iggy," I said. "I'm an inventor."

51
00:03:58.978 --> 00:04:01.575
"And I'm Molly," said Molly.

52
00:04:01.576 --> 00:04:04.332
"I'm just a regular person."

53
00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:08.196
"We're writing a story in school," I explained.

54
00:04:08.197 --> 00:04:12.458
"And we can't think of a good plot," added Molly.

55
00:04:12.459 --> 00:04:16.203
Mrs. Mackey's eyes lit up.

56
00:04:16.204 --> 00:04:19.867
"Here's what you have to do," she said.

57
00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:24.424
"Ask yourself what the character wants more than anything in the world.

58
00:04:24.425 --> 00:04:28.640
And then give her a huge problem to solve."

59
00:04:28.641 --> 00:04:33.628
Somehow Mrs. Mackey's words sounded familiar.

60
00:04:33.629 --> 00:04:35.996
Then I realized why.

61
00:04:35.997 --> 00:04:37.960
It was just like my life!

62
00:04:37.961 --> 00:04:41.831
I always wanted to invent things to help people.

63
00:04:41.832 --> 00:04:44.488
And I always had a huge problem:

64
00:04:44.489 --> 00:04:50.676
my inventions turned out to be flops!
